{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nr=json.load(open('../research.json'));a=r['artifacts'][0];cid=r['candidates'][0]['id'];run=r['assessments'][0]['experiment_check_id']\nss=['S-init','S-members','S-phase1','S-bcast','S-ballot','S-recovery','S-defaults','S-wire','S-rpc','S-send','S-receive','S-messages']\nitem=dict(aspect='checker_correspondence',status='no_issue_found',source_ids=ss,rationale='Reviewed the fixed v1 harness and plan, accepted C-prepare-vballot-preservation v1, and raw CheckRun '+run+'. The written duty is exact preservation of the producer-reported VBallot through valid same-version RPC transfer, not agreement or progress. S-recovery handlePrepare constructs VBallot from inst.vbal and handlePrepareReply uses it for highest-value-ballot selection; S-messages distinguishes it from Ballot. Thus the producer/consumer relation supplies the local requirement independently of the implementation discrepancy. The fixed oracle compares decoded.vballot with produced.expected_vballot for scenario/acceptor/replica/instance, with produced explicitly selected as admission_alias; VBallot is not a correlation key. In owner_1 the raw prerequisite has acceptor=2, replica=1, instance=0, Ballot=3, Status=2 and expected_vballot=1; the uniquely matched later result has the same identity/Ballot/Status but vballot=0. owner_0 separately has expected/observed 0 and Ballot=5. Both observations are complete and parsed without errors; tests_passed means diagnostics completed, while the property comparison is violated. Constructor adaptation was checked against S-init/S-members: N=3 F=1, empty bounded rows, -1 prefixes, Thrifty and Dreply true, volatile state and fixed peer order. startPhase1 generates an initial owner-ID PreAccept; emitted bytes reach the selected distinct acceptor and establish PREACCEPTED_EQ and vbal. A distinct coordinator generates a higher Prepare through startRecoveryForInstance; acceptor handles it and emits bytes via real SendMsg/Marshal. The helper uses the actual registered New()/Unmarshal path and checks complete byte consumption. Producer-state sampling is faithful because handlePrepare directly copies those fields without further mutation; no concurrent handlers/executor run. The driver does not inject a fabricated PrepareReply or substitute its compared VBallot. Buffer transport and serial delivery select valid local calls without requiring arbitrary reordering, dropping fields, or overriding protocol logic. The coordinator recovery trigger is invoked directly, not a witnessed executor timer; that is a boundary of this explicitly local valid-message codec obligation, not an asserted timed global history. Pending unselected messages do not affect this completed transfer. The full PrepareReply codec omits VBallot; fresh allocation leaves it at zero. Neither exact request Ballot preservation nor other payload checks reconstruct the distinct provenance field before the recovery consumer.',counterevidence=['The zero-ballot case satisfies the equality; the finding is not that every PrepareReply changes VBallot.','Request Ballot, Status, Seq, commands and dependencies passed transport diagnostics; request-ballot matching remains a separate protection.','Self PrepareReply construction does not cross this codec, so the experiment does not claim all recovery support is corrupted.'],limitations=['No execution of handlePrepareReply, selected-value difference, conflicting decision, application result or whole-cluster safety/liveness consequence.','No reconstruction of the executor history that learned/requested the missing instance; direct valid-message entry isolates transport responsibility.','Only two initial owner-ballot cases in N=3; no malformed input, crash restart, concurrent read or shutdown claim.'],report_title='PrepareReply 传输丢失值轮次',report_answer='实际执行中，同一实例的 PrepareReply 在发送端对应 VBallot=1，解码后变为 0；零值对照保持为 0。该证据支持局部 RPC 值轮次保留责任的反例，尚未证明集群决策分歧。')\nfeedback=dict(ref_ids=[run,a['id'],cid,'B-wire','B-prepare','B-select','F-prepare','S-wire','S-recovery'],answered='The fixed check observed complete loss of nonzero PrepareReply value provenance at the RPC codec boundary: owner_1 expected 1, decoded 0; owner_0 expected and decoded 0. Correspondence review finds the comparison applicable to the local transport preservation duty.',remaining=['Investigate independent recovery support-selection and accepted-status preservation questions; a broader decision consequence would need its own legal history and proposition.'],understanding='updated',rationale='This resolves the selected codec discriminator without treating a local transport discrepancy as a cluster agreement witness.',question_updates={cid:dict(unknowns=['Broader selected-value or agreement consequences require additional legal-history work and are not established by this local codec comparison.'],resume_conditions=[])})\njson.dump(dict(action='review',artifact_id=a['id'],rationale='Review the actual fixed inputs, completed raw comparisons and local interface responsibility; retain zero-case counterevidence and wider-history limits.',review_items=[item],feedback=feedback),open('wire_review_submission.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-06_12-07-37-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run --submission wire_review_submission.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
